<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
     Local manifest for malbec (Lenovo TB390FU) on LineageOS 23.2.

     Copy to .repo/local_manifests/malbec.xml in a fresh checkout, then
     `repo sync`.

     ⚠️ WHY THIS FILE EXISTS INSTEAD OF `breakfast malbec`

     `lineage.dependencies` is the LineageOS-native mechanism and it CANNOT work
     for a personal fork. vendor/lineage/build/tools/roomservice.py hardcodes the
     LineageOS organisation in two places:

         line 222   'name': f'LineageOS/{repo_name}'
         line 327   git ls-remote https://:@github.com/LineageOS/<repo_name>

     and the `remote` escape at lines 226 to 233 applies only to `aosp-*`
     remotes; other remote names are ignored and the LineageOS-prefixed project
     remains. So a dependency written as

         "repository": "suddenBook/proprietary_vendor_lenovo_malbec"

     is probed as `LineageOS/suddenBook/proprietary_vendor_lenovo_malbec`, comes
     back with no branches, and roomservice.py line 349 exits with

         Default revision lineage-23.2 not found in ... Bailing.

     Moving the four custom repos onto the `lineage-23.2` branch was a real and
     separate bug, and fixing it was necessary but not sufficient: the
     organisation prefix cannot be fixed from the device tree at all. Hence this
     file.

     `lineage.dependencies` is retained as machine-readable dependency intent,
     but it is not a working bootstrap file. If the repositories ever move to
     LineageOS, their `suddenBook/` prefixes must also be removed there.

     ⚠️ AFTER SYNCING, BEFORE BUILDING

     vendor/gapps uses Git LFS and `repo sync` does not smudge it. GmsCore.apk
     (175 MB) and Velvet.apk (254 MB) remain pointer files if LFS is not enabled
     and the objects are not pulled. Left that way, the build can still appear
     successful while the device has no usable Play Services.

     Run the two LFS commands from the device tree's README (`git lfs install`
     with the local flag, then `git lfs pull`). `git lfs pull`
     on its own prints "Skipping object checkout, Git LFS is not installed for
     this repository" and EXITS 0. work/scripts/01-lfs-check.sh is tree-wide and
     is a pre-flight in 40-build.sh, so a build cannot start with a pointer.

     ⚠️ ABOUT vendor/gapps

     This device ships full GMS (owner's decision, session 23). LineageOS's own
     mechanism — WITH_GMS=true plus vendor/partner_gms — is not usable outside
     the official build farm: partner_gms is not in the public manifest and
     LineageOS/android_vendor_partner_gms is not a public repository. MindTheGapps
     is the maintained public equivalent; branch `baklava` is Android 16, which
     is what LineageOS 23.x is. It MUST be checked out at exactly `vendor/gapps`:
     its common-vendor.mk inherits `vendor/gapps/common/common-vendor.mk` by
     absolute path.

     These custom projects use moving branch revisions. That is deliberate for
     normal development and GMS security updates, but it means two syncs a month
     apart need not produce the same image. Pin every project to a SHA for an
     immutable source selection.
-->
<manifest>
  <remote name="suddenBook"
          fetch="https://github.com/suddenBook"
          revision="refs/heads/lineage-23.2" />

  <remove-project name="LineageOS/android_packages_apps_Launcher3" />

  <project path="packages/apps/Launcher3"
           name="android_packages_apps_Launcher3"
           remote="suddenBook"
           groups="pdk-cw-tvc,pdk-fs,sysui-studio" />

  <project path="device/lenovo/malbec"
           name="android_device_lenovo_malbec"
           remote="suddenBook" />

  <project path="device/lenovo/malbec-kernel"
           name="android_device_lenovo_malbec-kernel"
           remote="suddenBook" />

  <project path="vendor/lenovo/malbec"
           name="proprietary_vendor_lenovo_malbec"
           remote="suddenBook" />

  <remote name="mindthegapps"
          fetch="https://gitlab.com/MindTheGapps" />

  <project path="vendor/gapps"
           name="vendor_gapps"
           remote="mindthegapps"
           revision="baklava"
           clone-depth="1" />
</manifest>
